.TH LUMOS\-MD 1 2026-11-24 "lumos\-md 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumos\-md \- Markdown editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lumos\-md
.RI [ file " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lumos\-md
edits Markdown files as source text, with syntax colours and format
commands. It follows CommonMark and GitHub Flavored Markdown. Every edit
is a text edit.
.PP
Each
.I file
given opens in its own tab, after the tabs of the last session. Without
one, the tabs of the last session open, or one empty document. If
lumos\-md is already running, the files open in its window, and this
start exits.
.PP
A few seconds after an edit, the unsaved text goes to a draft file.
After a crash, the next start offers to recover it.
.PP
When an open file changes on disk, lumos\-md loads it again as one
undo step and says so in the status bar; Undo gives the old text back.
A tab with unsaved changes asks first: Show diff (both texts side by
side, to merge them), Save as shown, Load changes or Cancel. A deleted
or moved file asks: Keep in editor or Close. Save asks before it
writes over a file that changed on disk.
.PP
A file without write access opens for edits as usual. The window title
shows [Read\-Only], and Save opens Save As.
.PP
View \-> Show Preview shows the current tab as HTML, right of the editor.
It follows the text and the scroll position of the editor. The buttons
on the bar between them give the preview or the editor the full width.
A click on a link opens it. Raw HTML in a note does not show, and
pictures load only from local files.
.PP
View \-> Theme picks the colours: Default (the colours of the desktop),
Light grey, Gruvbox, Dark, Dark blue-grey or Dark slate (the last four
are dark). View \-> Paper look works only with a light theme.
.PP
Edit \-> Paste from HTML (Ctrl+Alt+V) pastes a copy from a web page as
Markdown: headings, lists, quotes, code blocks, tables, links, and bold,
italic or code text. One undo removes the whole paste. In a code block
or a table, it pastes the plain text.
.PP
AI agents (MCP): with Tools \-> Enable MCP Server on, an agent can list the
open files and read their text, with unsaved changes. It reads a file
before it changes it, then writes the file with its own tools; the
change shows as a change on disk. An agent can also show a file
(only *.md, *.markdown and *.txt files): it opens in a tab, that tab becomes the current one and the window is
raised (on Wayland the desktop may only mark it as urgent). With a line
number, the cursor goes to the start of that line and the line scrolls
to the middle of the view. The keyboard focus does not move. In the agent's settings, add the
command
.B lumos\-md \-\-mcp
as a stdio MCP server.
Any program of the same user can then read the open files, also text
that is not saved, and open files in tabs, but only in the folders of
Tools \-> MCP Allowed Folders (none by default). The switch is off by
default.
.PP
Help \-> Features lists what lumos\-md does and does not do; Help \-> MCP Server
shows how to set up an agent. The pages open as read\-only tabs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Run as the MCP server for an AI agent, over standard input and output.
The agent starts it; it opens no window and talks to the running
lumos\-md.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-dir " dir"
With
.BR \-\-mcp :
the socket folder chosen in Tools \-> MCP Socket Folder, for an agent in
a sandbox that cannot see the default socket.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \(ti/.config/lumos\-md/lumos\-md.ini
The settings. For debug lines in the log, add
.B debug=true
under
.B [log]
in this file.
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/state/lumos\-md/lumos\-md.log
The log, one line per event. At 1 MB it moves to
.IR lumos\-md.log.1 .
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/state/lumos\-md/open\-tabs
The open tabs, for the next start.
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/state/lumos\-md/drafts/
The drafts of unsaved text.
.TP
.I \(ti/.lumos\-md/
If
.I \(ti/.lumos\-md/lumos\-md.ini
exists, the settings, the log, the open tabs and the drafts are in this
directory instead. To change the directory, close lumos\-md first, then
move the files by hand: lumos\-md writes the settings when its window
closes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/lumos\-md/help/
The pages of the Help menu.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Replaces
.I \(ti/.config
in the paths above.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Replaces
.I \(ti/.local/state
in the paths above.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/confund0/lumos\-md/issues
